# Line endings. Everything text is LF in the repo and LF on checkout, on every
# platform. Added 2026-08-27 after CRLF crept into three Python files and made
# their diffs unreadable (550 changed lines for a 4-line edit).
* text=auto eol=lf

# Shell scripts and macOS .command wrappers MUST be LF. bash fails with a
# "\r: command not found" style error if these ever pick up CRLF.
*.sh        text eol=lf
*.command   text eol=lf
*.py        text eol=lf

# Windows batch files are left exactly as they are, no normalization either
# way. These are slated to be retooled; revisit then.
*.bat       -text

# Data exports are gitignored, but if one is ever force-added, do not let git
# rewrite bytes inside a student data file.
*.csv       -text
